---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
const faqSchema = faqPageSchema([
  { question: 'Legal use boundary', answer: 'Authorization defaults, no unauthorized commercial how-tos, clean-room vs closed apps.' },
]);
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Legal use boundary FAQ | rea.run"
  description="Authorization defaults, no unauthorized commercial how-tos, clean-room vs closed apps."
  path="/faq/legal-boundary/"
  schema={faqSchema}
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>

    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">FAQ · P0</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">Legal use boundary</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">What rea.run will and will not help you do with REA.</p>
    <h2>Default posture</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>REA runs <strong>locally</strong> against artifacts you supply. You are responsible for having the right to analyze them.</li>
      <li>We do not operate a upload-your-binary service on rea.run, and we do not endorse illegal use.</li>
      <li>Guides assume authorization: your builds, OSS under compatible licenses, malware in approved labs, or written permission.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>“Can I reverse this commercial app?”</h2>
    <p><strong>We do not publish how-tos for unauthorized reverse engineering of commercial software.</strong> Community channels occasionally ask about named closed products; those threads are demand signals for a boundary reminder — not lesson plans. We will not turn them into step-by-step attack recipes.</p>
    <h2>Clean-room / open companions</h2>
    <p>Learning patterns from public standards, open-source companions, or publisher-authorized SDKs is different from stripping protection on a proprietary binary you do not own. When in doubt, stop and get counsel or permission.</p>
    <h2>Related on this site</h2>
    <p><a href="/compliance/">Compliance</a> · <a href="/showcase/">Showcase</a> (authorized / public cases only)</p>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/README.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Upstream README disclaimer</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1343" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1343 — clean-room / boundary discussion theme</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/discussions/693" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Discussion #693 — unauthorized commercial ask (boundary signal only)</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/discussions/1115" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Discussion #1115 — unauthorized commercial ask (boundary signal only)</a></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
